--- body ---
## Context

`pyproject.toml` ships 13 flat top-level modules (`[tool.setuptools] py-modules`). Installing DOIfetch
(`uv tool install`, `pip install`) therefore puts modules named `config`, `utils` and `fetch` at the top
level of the target environment, where they shadow or are shadowed by any other package using those
names. Moving only the `fetch_*.py` files into a `fetchers/` folder would tidy the root but leave that
namespace problem in place, so the whole code base moves into one package.

Sequenced after 0004 on purpose: 0004 removes the per-fetcher file-naming code, so the fetchers are
thinner when they move and 0004 is not rebased across a rename. 0005 (dependency slimming) also edits
`pyproject.toml` and must have landed first.

## Target layout

```
src/doifetch/
  __init__.py
  cli.py          # today's fetch.py
  config.py  utils.py  pdf_utils.py  zotero.py
  sources/        # crossref, unpaywall, hal, istex, ezproxy, libgen, scihub, url
tests/
```

`sources/` matches the existing `--source` CLI flag, so the `fetch_` prefix is dropped
(`sources/crossref.py`).

## Actions
1. `git mv` the modules into `src/doifetch/` and `src/doifetch/sources/`; rewrite imports in code and tests.
2. `pyproject.toml`: package discovery under `src/`, entry point `doifetch = "doifetch.cli:main"`,
   drop `py-modules` and the pytest `pythonpath = ["."]`.
3. Drop the per-source script entry points (`uv run fetch_crossref.py …`, README l. 176–181): they
   duplicate `doifetch --source X`. Each source stays runnable as `python -m doifetch.sources.<name>`
   only if that costs nothing; otherwise drop its `main()`.
4. Update README (module list, usage, development).

## Invariants
- No behaviour change: same CLI flags, same outputs. Pure move plus import rewrite.
- Validate by the suite and by a fresh-clone `uv run doifetch --help` and one mocked single-DOI fetch,
  not by the green suite alone.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] No top-level module other than `doifetch` is installed
- [ ] `uv run doifetch --help` works from a fresh clone
- [ ] Existing test suite passes unchanged in substance (imports only)
- [ ] README reflects the new layout and invocation
